## 🛠️ Validation Utilities (Sample Implementation)

```javascript
// Common validation utilities
const ENV_VALIDATORS = {
  // AWS
  AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID: /^AKIA[A-Z0-9]{16}$/,
  AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY: /^[0-9a-f]{40}$/i,

  // Stripe
  STRIPE_SECRET_KEY: /^sk_(live|test)_[a-f0-9]{24}$/,
  STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY: /^pk_(live|test)_[a-f0-9]{24}$/,
  STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET: /^whsec_[a-f0-9]{32}$/,

  // JWT
  JWT_SECRET: (val) => val && val.length >= 32,

  // Database & Email
  DB_URL: /^(mongodb)(:\/\/.+)?@?.+\/.+$/,
  REDIS_URL: /^redis(s)?:\/\/([-a-zA-Z0-9.]+)(:([0-9]+))?\/?$/i,
  EMAIL_HOST: /^([a-zA-Z0-9]([a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}[a-zA-Z0-9])?\.)+[a-zA-Z]{2,}$/,
  EMAIL_PORT: /^[0-9]{4}$/,
  EMAIL_USER: /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/,

  // OAuth
  GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET: /^[0-9a-zA-Z+/]{32}={0,2}$/,
  FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET: /^[0-9a-f]{32}$/i,

  // URLs & Origins
  STRIPE_OR_PAYPAL_API_URL: /^https:\/\/api(-m)?\.(\stripe|paypal)\.com\/.+$/,
  CLOUDFRONT_PLUS: /^https?:\/\/.*\.[a-zA-Z]{2,}/,
  FRONTEND_URL: /^https?:\/\/.*\.[a-zA-Z]{2,}/,
  CORS_ORIGIN: /^https?:\/\/[^\/\s]+$/,
  ALLOWED_ORIGINS: /^https?:\/\/[^\s,]+(,[^\s,]+)*$/,

  // Feature Flags
  FEATURE_FLAG: /^(!)?(true|false|1|0)$/,
};
```

---

## 📋 Quick Reference Cheat Sheet

| Category | Pattern Examples |
|----------|------------------|
| AWS Keys | `AKIA` + 16 chars / 40 hex chars |
| Stripe Keys | `sk_live_` or `sk_test_` + 24 hex chars |
| Stripe Publishable | `pk_live_` or `pk_test_` + 24 hex chars |
| Stripe Webhook | `whsec_` + 32 hex chars |
| AWS Secret | 40 hex characters (A-F, 0-9) |
| JWT Secret | >= 32 characters |
| Database Password | >= 8 chars, mixed case, numbers, symbols |
| OAuth Client Secret | 32 chars (base64/URL-safe) |
| WhatsApp | Short (15-16 chars) |
| Twilio SID | `AC` + 32 alphanumeric chars |
| Twilio Auth Token | 32 alphanumeric chars |
| SMS | 6 digits (SIM provider) |
| Cache (Memcache) | >= 8 chars, mixed type |

